  "notes": "{貧|まず}しい is an i-adjective describing poverty or insufficiency.\n\nFORMS:\n- Adverbial: {貧|まず}しく\n- Noun form: {貧|まず}しさ (poverty, poorness)\n\nTWO MEANINGS:\n1. Financially poor: {貧|まず}しい⟦{家庭|かてい}→家庭：12315_katei⟧ (poor family)\n2. Lacking quality: ⟦{発想|はっそう}→発想：04309_hassou⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{貧|まず}しい (lacking imagination)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {貧|まず}しい⟦{生活|せいかつ}→生活：01443_seikatsu⟧: impoverished life\n- {貧|まず}しい⟦{国|くに}→国：02204_kuni⟧: poor country\n- ⟦{心|こころ}→心：01321_kokoro⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{貧|まず}しい: spiritually poor/petty\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{貧乏|びんぼう}→貧乏：19466_binbou⟧: poor (noun/na-adjective, more colloquial)\n- ⟦{貧困|ひんこん}→貧困：04836_hinkon⟧: poverty (formal noun)\n- ⟦{裕福|ゆうふく}→裕福：14041_yuufuku⟧: wealthy\n- ⟦{金持|かねも}ち→金持ち：02993_kanemochi⟧: rich person",
